*** Keywords ***
General_SiSo_Auto_RAT_Reset
    [Documentation]   Test Case provides possibility to perform L3 call after RAT reset by passing ${throughputs} argument
    ...               In case of multiRAT configuration:
    ...               - the test resets one RAT at a time and waits until it is onAir then resets the next one
    ...               - if resetting RATs in the correct order is required, create a string looks like python list
    ...                 with RATs in the specified order and pass it to the ${rat_type} argument e.g. rat_type=[LTE, NR]
    ...
    ...               In case of custom configuration:
    ...               Test allows to pass to the ${rat_type} argument a dictionary with RATs and their reset options
    ...               e.g. first create a dictionary in your test suite in the ***Variable*** section.
    ...               ${rat_type}  {'NR':{'reset_type': 'hard', 'graceful_cell_shutdown': True, 'l3call_in_background': True},
    ...               ...           'LTE':{'reset_type': 'soft','l3call_in_background': 'MRBTS-40615/LNBTS-40615/NRCELL-10'},
    ...               ...           'WCDMA': {'reset_type': 'hard', 'graceful_cell_shutdown': False, 'l3call_in_background': False},
    ...               ...           'GSM': {'reset_type': 'soft', 'graceful_cell_shutdown': False, 'l3call_in_background': False}}
    ...               All options keys like 'reset_type', 'graceful_cell_shutdown', 'l3call_in_background' are mandatory
    ...               and should be provided for each RAT. If some of the options are not provided, default values from
    ...               the arguments from the main TC will be used. e.g
    ...               ${rat_type}  {'NR':{'l3call_in_background': True},
    ...               ...           'LTE':{'l3call_in_background': 'MRBTS-40615/LNBTS-40615/NRCELL-10'},
    ...               'NR' - will be reset with default values for reset_type='Soft', graceful_cell_shutdown=False
    ...               and l3call_in_background will be executed but to random cell from RAT not affected by reset
    ...               'LTE' - same as above but with l3call_in_background to specified cell
    ...
    ...               ARGS:
    ...                - rat_type: name of RAT(s) to reset (NR, LTE, WCDMA, GSM);
    ...                            defaults to ${None} which means that all RATs will be tested
    ...                            supports list of RATs which can be pass directly to arg e.g. rat_type=[NR, LTE]
    ...                            or dictionary with RATs and their reset options
    ...                - reset_type: type of RAT reset; defaults to soft; available options (soft/hard)
    ...                - graceful_cell_shutdown: additional option when resetting RAT; defaults to ${False}
    ...                - l3call_in_background: additional option when resetting RAT; defaults to ${True} which means
    ...                                        that L3 call will be allowed in background to random cell.
    ...                                        Finall execution L3call in background will depend on the fulfillment
    ...                                        of all conditions in the KW 'Check If L3call In Background Allowed'
    ...                  If set to ${False} l3call in background will not be executed even if custom config is provided
    ...                - l3call_after_rat_reset: if set to ${True} L3call will be executed after RAT reset
    ...                                          defaults to ${False}
    ...
    ...                !!! IMPORTANT !! When executing test case with L3 call, if your testline is connected to programmable
    ...                                 attenuator please ensure that all relevant ports are unattenuated as this test case
    ...                                 will not handle attenuation.
    ...                - called_cells_distnames: CONFIGURATION distnames of cells that will be called, after RAT reset
    ...                               if not given, list of all cells on testline will be determined and called
    ...                - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for each cell identified by
    ...                               it's nrCellIdentity for NR cells, eutranCellId for LTE cells, wnCelId for WCDMA cells;
    ...                               defaults to None (L3 call will not be executed).
    ...                               Example:
    ...                               {
    ...                                   '827736065':
    ...                                        {
    ...                                            'throughput':
    ...                                                {
    ...                                                    'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                    'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                },
    ...                                            'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                        },
    ...                               }
    ...                - protocol: data transfer protocol; defaults to UDP.
    ...                - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer; defaults to 4M.
    ...                - tput_verification_via_btslog: True - throughput verification will be performed using btslog
    ...                                                False - throuput verification will be performed using iperf; defaults to False
    ...                - ue_network_modes: dict with UE serial numbers and desired network modes e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only"}
    ...                                    possible UE network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE
    ...                                    when using more than one UE please make sure that the modes you choose are either all
    ...                                    with "_only" suffix or all "NR_LTE" as it is not yet possible to mix those.
    ...                                    mandatory for SA+NSA setups, defaults to None
    ...                - ues_and_cells: dict with UE serial numbers and lists of configuration distnames of cells to which they
    ...                                 can be attached e.g. {"SN1234": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-1", "MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-3"],
    ...                                                       "SN5678": ["MRBTS-50146/NRBTS-1/NRCELL-5"]}
    ...                                 defaults to ${None} which means that all UEs will be attached to all cells.
    ...                                 when given, listed cells will be called in pairs with specified UEs, if there are more
    ...                                 cells on the setup that were not mentioned in the list, they will be called with all UEs
    ...                - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred

    [Arguments]        ${rat_type}=${None}
    ...                ${reset_type}=soft
    ...                ${graceful_cell_shutdown}=${False}
    ...                ${l3call_in_background}=${False}
    ...                ${called_cells_distnames}=${None}
    ...                ${throughputs}=${None}
    ...                ${protocol}=udp
    ...                ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...                ${tput_verification_via_btslog}=${False}
    ...                ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...                ${ues_and_cells}=${None}
    ...                ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    Set test variables

    ${bts_type}=                                    hwpta_testline.get_type_of_setup
    ${connection_alias}=                            connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    ...                                             bts_type=${bts_type}
    ${cell_distnames_per_rat}=                      admin_info_model.get_cell_distnames_from_configured_rats
    ...                                             connection=${connection_alias}

    Check actRATResetEnhancement Parameter And Set It To True If Disabled
    ...                                             connection_alias=${connection_alias}

    ${rats_dict}=                                   Prepare RATs With Reset Options
    ...                                             rat_type=${rat_type}
    ...                                             reset_type=${reset_type}
    ...                                             graceful_cell_shutdown=${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                                             l3call_in_background=${l3call_in_background}
    ...                                             cells_per_rat=${cell_distnames_per_rat}

    Robot Log Step    Test will perform RAT reset for following RATs with the specified reset options: ${rats_dict}

    FOR    ${rat}    ${reset_options}    IN ZIP     ${rats_dict.keys()}    ${rats_dict.values()}
        Robot Log Step                              Starting ${reset_type} ${rat} RAT reset test ...
        ${reset_type}=                              Set Variable   ${reset_options['reset_type']}
        ${graceful_cell_shutdown}=                  Set Variable   ${reset_options['graceful_cell_shutdown']}
        ${bg_l3call_from_dict}=                     Set Variable   ${reset_options['l3call_in_background']}

        ${env_vrf}=                                 Get Library Instance    rat_env_vrf
        Call method                                 ${env_vrf}              initialize
        ...                                         reset_rat=${rat}
        ...                                         reset_type=${reset_type}
        ...                                         connection_alias=${connection_alias}
        ...                                         called_cell_distnames=${called_cells_distnames}

        Run keyword if                              ${throughputs}
        ...                                         Execute L3 call
        ...                                         cells_distnames=${env_vrf.get_rat_reset_cell_distnames()}
        ...                                         throughputs=${throughputs}
        ...                                         protocol=${protocol}
        ...                                         udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
        ...                                         tput_verification_via_btslog=${tput_verification_via_btslog}
        ...                                         ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
        ...                                         ues_and_cells=${ues_and_cells}
        ...                                         ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}

        ${background_l3call}    ${bg_l3call_cell}   Check If L3call In Background Allowed
        ...                                         rats_dict=${rats_dict}
        ...                                         bg_l3call_from_dict=${bg_l3call_from_dict}
        ...                                         l3call_in_background=${l3call_in_background}
        ...                                         env_vrf=${env_vrf}

        Run keyword if                              ${background_l3call}
        ...   Run keywords                          Allow Alarms Before L3 Call In Background
        ...   AND                                   call_manager.Start L3 Call In Background
        ...                                         called_cell=${bg_l3call_cell}
        ...                                         direction=DL
        ...                                         duration=forever
        ...                                         throughputs=${throughputs}
        ...                                         protocol=${protocol}
        ...                                         udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
        ...                                         ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
        ...                                         ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}
        ...    AND                                  Set test variable   ${is_background_l3call}    ${True}
        ...    AND                                  Set test variable   ${bg_l3call_cell}          ${bg_l3call_cell}
        ...    AND       call method                ${env_vrf}    update_statuses_after_l3call_prep
        ...    ELSE      Robot Log Result           L3call in background NOT allowed

        Allow Alarms Before RAT Reset

        ${reset_rat_background_task}                Perform RAT Reset In Background
        ...                                         rat=${rat}
        ...                                         reset_type=${reset_type}
        ...                                         graceful_cell_shutdown=${graceful_cell_shutdown}

        Verify Env After RAT Reset And Wait For Affected Components
        ...                                         env_vrf=${env_vrf}
        ...                                         connection_alias=${connection_alias}

        Disallow Alarms After RAT Reset

        Run keyword if                              ${is_background_l3call}
        ...  Run keywords                           call_manager.Stop Background L3 Call and Verify Results
        ...                                         called_cell=${bg_l3call_cell}
        ...  AND                                    Set test variable   ${is_background_l3call}    ${False}
        ...  AND                                    Disallow Alarms after L3 Call In Background

        Run keyword if                              ${throughputs}
        ...                                         Execute L3 call
        ...                                         cells_distnames=${env_vrf.get_rat_reset_cell_distnames()}
        ...                                         throughputs=${throughputs}
        ...                                         protocol=${protocol}
        ...                                         udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
        ...                                         tput_verification_via_btslog=${tput_verification_via_btslog}
        ...                                         ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
        ...                                         ues_and_cells=${ues_and_cells}
        ...                                         ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}
        Robot Log Step                              Successfully executed ${rat} ${reset_type} RAT reset!\n
    END

    [Teardown]                                      Run Keywords
    ...  Run keyword if  ${is_background_l3call}    Stop Background L3 Call And Unblock All Cells
    ...                                             called_cell=${bg_l3call_cell}
    ...                                             connection=${connection_alias}
    ...  AND
    ...  Run keyword if  ${is_param_recommissioned}
    ...                                             config_operations.set_parameter_value
    ...                                             dist_name=MRBTS-{}/MNL-1/MNLENT-1/FEATCADM-1
    ...                                             param_name=actRatResetEnhancement
    ...                                             param_value=false
    ...  AND                                        admin_info_model.collect_background_keyword_result
    ...                                             task=${reset_rat_background_task}


Check actRATResetEnhancement Parameter And Set It To True If Disabled
    [Documentation]    Check if 'actRatResetEnhancement' parameter is set to True
    ...                If not, set it to True
    [Arguments]        ${connection_alias}

    config_operations.connect                       alias=${connection_alias}
    ${initial_param_value}=                         config_operations.get_parameter_value
    ...                                             dist_name=MRBTS-{}/MNL-1/MNLENT-1/FEATCADM-1
    ...                                             param_name=actRatResetEnhancement

    Run keyword if                                  '${initial_param_value}'=='false'
    ...    Run keywords     Robot Log Operation     Perform recommissioning parameter 'actRatResetEnhancement' to 'true'
    ...    AND                                      config_operations.set_parameter_value
    ...                                             dist_name=MRBTS-{}/MNL-1/MNLENT-1/FEATCADM-1
    ...                                             param_name=actRatResetEnhancement
    ...                                             param_value=true
    ...    AND                                      Set test variable    ${is_param_recommissioned}     ${True}


Prepare RATs With Reset Options
    [Documentation]    Prepare RATs dictionary with reset options
    [Arguments]        ${rat_type}
    ...                ${reset_type}
    ...                ${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                ${l3call_in_background}
    ...                ${cells_per_rat}

    ${default_options}=    Create dictionary        reset_type=${reset_type}
    ...                                             graceful_cell_shutdown=${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                                             l3call_in_background=${l3call_in_background}
    ${rats}=               run keyword if           """${rat_type}"""=="""${None}"""
    ...                    get dictionary keys      ${cells_per_rat}
    ...                    ELSE                     Set variable   ${rat_type}
    ${custom_config}                                Check If Custom Config Provided
    ...                                             rat_type=${rat_type}

    ${rats_dict}=          run keyword if           ${custom_config}
    ...                                             Verify Custom RATs Config And Add Defaults If Needed
    ...                                             rat_type=${rats}
    ...                                             reset_type=${reset_type}
    ...                                             l3call_in_background=${l3call_in_background}
    ...                                             graceful_cell_shutdown=${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                                             cells_per_rat=${cells_per_rat}
    ...                    ELSE                     Prepare RATs With Params Provided In Args
    ...                                             rat_type=${rats}
    ...                                             reset_type=${reset_type}
    ...                                             l3call_in_background=${l3call_in_background}
    ...                                             graceful_cell_shutdown=${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                                             cells_per_rat=${cells_per_rat}

   [Return]            ${rats_dict}


Set Test Variables
    [Documentation]    Set test variables for Teardown purposes
    set test variable                               ${is_param_recommissioned}          ${False}
    set test variable                               ${is_background_l3call}             ${False}


Check If L3call In Background Allowed
    [Documentation]    Check if L3call in background is allowed
    [Arguments]        ${rats_dict}
    ...                ${bg_l3call_from_dict}
    ...                ${l3call_in_background}
    ...                ${env_vrf}

    ${bg_l3call_cell}=            Run keyword if    """${bg_l3call_from_dict}"""=="""${True}"""
    ...                           Set Variable      ${env_vrf.get_random_callable_cell_distname()}
    ...    ELSE                   Set Variable      ${bg_l3call_from_dict}

    ${is_multirat}=               Evaluate          len(${rats_dict}) > 1
    ${bg_l3call}=                 Evaluate          ${l3call_in_background} == True
    ${bg_l3call_from_dict}=       Evaluate          """${bg_l3call_cell}""" != False
    ${is_callable}=               Evaluate          """${bg_l3call_cell}""" in ${env_vrf.get_callable_cell_distnames()}

    ${l3call_allowed}=  Evaluate   ${is_multirat} and ${bg_l3call} and ${bg_l3call_from_dict} and ${is_callable}

    [Return]            ${l3call_allowed}       ${bg_l3call_cell}


Prepare RATs With Params Provided In Args
    [Documentation]    Prepare RATs dictionary with reset options provided in arguments
    [Arguments]        ${rat_type}
    ...                ${reset_type}
    ...                ${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                ${l3call_in_background}
    ...                ${cells_per_rat}

    ${rat_type}            evaluate      list("""${rat_type}""".translate({ord(i): None for i in '[]" \\''}).split(","))
    ${default_options}=    Create dictionary        reset_type=${reset_type}
    ...                                             graceful_cell_shutdown=${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                                             l3call_in_background=${l3call_in_background}
    ${rats_dict}=          Evaluate                 {rat: ${default_options} for rat in ${rat_type}}

    Log          ${rats_dict}
    [Return]     ${rats_dict}


Verify Custom RATs Config And Add Defaults If Needed
    [Documentation]    Verify custom RATs config provided as a dictionary and add defaults if not present
    [Arguments]        ${rat_type}
    ...                ${reset_type}
    ...                ${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                ${l3call_in_background}
    ...                ${cells_per_rat}

    ${custom_rats_dict}=         Evaluate           dict(${rat_type})
    ${mandatory_with_defaults}=  Create dictionary  reset_type=${reset_type}
    ...                                             graceful_cell_shutdown=${graceful_cell_shutdown}
    ...                                             l3call_in_background=${l3call_in_background}

    FOR    ${rat}  ${options}    IN ZIP             ${custom_rats_dict.keys()}    ${custom_rats_dict.values()}
        Verify Mandatory And Add Defaults           rat=${rat}
        ...                                         custom_rat_options=${options}
        ...                                         mandatory_with_defaults=${mandatory_with_defaults}
        ...                                         custom_rats_dict=${custom_rats_dict}
    END
    Log         ${custom_rats_dict}
    [Return]    ${custom_rats_dict}


Verify Mandatory And Add Defaults
    [Documentation]    Verify mandatory options and add defaults if needed
    [Arguments]        ${rat}
    ...                ${custom_rat_options}
    ...                ${mandatory_with_defaults}
    ...                ${custom_rats_dict}

    FOR    ${m_key}    ${m_value}    IN ZIP    ${mandatory_with_defaults.keys()}    ${mandatory_with_defaults.values()}
        Run keyword if               '${m_key}' not in ${custom_rat_options}
        ...                          Set To Dictionary  ${custom_rats_dict}[${rat}]     ${m_key}    ${m_value}
    END


Check If Custom Config Provided
    [Documentation]    Checks if ${rat_type} is a dict, if 'True' custom config provided
